BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VCEE Seminar: Kristoffer Hvidberg (U Aarhus)
DTSTART:20251020T093000Z
DTEND:20251020T110000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T212450Z
UID:1nkdrfpk6ns6n7fluge11m5k90@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20250623T121127Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><u>Speaker:</u> </b><a href="https://kristofferhvidberg.com
 /" target="_blank">Kristoffer Hvidberg </a><br><br><b><u>Title:</u></b> 
 Preferences and Choice of Education<br><br><b><u>Abstract:</u></b> We inv
 estigate whether economic preferences influence educational choices indepe
 ndently of cognitive ability. Using incentivized experiments with over 4\,
 000 Danish 19-year-olds linked to administrative records\, we find that pa
 tience predicts enrollment in longer educational programs\, while risk ave
 rsion predicts selection into programs with lower earnings dispersion. Bot
 h effects persist after controlling for cognitive ability measured by GPA\
 , demographic characteristics\, and parental background. Our results demon
 strate that economic preferences explain variation in educational choices 
 beyond academic background and achievement\, with implications for underst
 anding human capital investment.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251103T080445Z
LOCATION:Oskar-Morgenstern-Platz 1\, Hörsaal 7\, 1st floor
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
